laude Code: `transcript_path` field should match actual storage location.\\n- Logs an info-level message (`agent.claudecode resolved transcript via fallback scan`) when the fallback fires, so the redirect is observable in `.entire/logs/`.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes how Claude Code hook events resolve `SessionRef` by falling back to a filesystem scan when the reported transcript path is missing, which could affect session selection if multiple projects contain the same session ID or if permissions differ.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Fixes Claude Code lifecycle event handling when `transcript_path` points at a non-existent worktree-derived location by resolving the canonical transcript path before emitting events.\\n> \\n> All hook parsers now set `SessionRef` via a new `resolveTranscriptPath` helper that first uses the reported path if it exists, otherwise scans `~/.claude/projects/*/<sessionID>.jsonl` for a match and logs an info message when the fallback is used. Adds unit tests covering the scan helper and resolver (passthrough, empty inputs, no-match/nonexistent base, and the worktree fallback scenario).\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 062641f28ee2a2219c6a88f86700e67a2b35f0c5. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\"number\":1159,\"title\":\"Fall back to scanning when Claude transcript_path is missing\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1159\"}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4756cd63-6aeb-4c6b-b998-ed1071a92d54","timestamp":"2026-05-08T15:11:16.663Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"{\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nFix dropped checkpoints when Claude Code runs inside its worktree feature (`.claude/worktrees/<branch>/`).\\n\\nClaude reports `transcript_path` encoded from the worktree CWD, e.g.\\n`~/.claude/projects/-Users-foo-Development-repo-